1. \( A_i \neq \varnothing \) for \( i = 1, 2, \cdots, n \);
2. \( A_i \cap A_j = \varnothing \);
3. \( \bigcup_{i=1}^{n} A_i = S \),

then \( A_1, A_2, \cdots, A_n \) are called a partition of set \( S \).

